64-bit atomics on ppc32 are libatomic calls, and the mfbt test programs
are not linked with LIBATOMIC_LIBS. Skip the 64-bit cases of
TestAtomicBitfields and TestAtomics there, and TestMPSCQueue, whose
ring buffer is built on std::atomic<uint64_t>, entirely.

diff --git mfbt/tests/TestAtomicBitfields.cpp mfbt/tests/TestAtomicBitfields.cpp
index 9f561c6..26bfe6f 100644
--- mfbt/tests/TestAtomicBitfields.cpp
+++ mfbt/tests/TestAtomicBitfields.cpp
@@ -172,7 +172,9 @@ GENERATE_TEST_JAMMED_WITH_FLAGS(32)
